posts.body:
Kupotepo said:
Thank you for sharing your resources with us. Your resources are really popular in another RPG forum and I am also remembering you have a store there too. Yeah, I am kind of the lurker fan of yours because I see your amazing resources.
Mmmmm, would you mind sharing what will you create next, so we are feeling hyped?
Click to expand...
I don't do any kind of external promotion on this forum. If anyone wants "more" then google will get you there. As for what I'll work on next, I'm still looking at the MZ graphics to see what might be useful for others. I'll be working through the RTP for a while -- then we'll see. Little things like Character edits (mostly doors) will come soon.
All RTP edits I do will be released on this site. I'd also like to take this opportunity to thank
@Cyanide
for helping me to understand tile art. Without her, none of these edits would be here. Other substantial inspirations of mine are
@Amysaurus
,
@Avery
, and PandaMaru. This community has been absolutely amazing.
(p.s. don't want to leave out the programmers --
@ct_bolt
and
@LTN Games
BIG UPS!
)

@Starbird_Resources
, thank you for all of the stuff you share on here.  You are very creative!
@Finnuval
, I'm sure the day will come.  There are usually good deals in the Spring, because of Golden Week.

wow, AWESOME stuff
@Starbird_Resources
!

Stained glass windows! These will make a magnificent cathedral to house that gorgeous organ (
@Avery
) gift. You must have been working on these for months.

Thank you for taking the time to leave such a kind comment
@JoePal
- made my day! And it counts double coming from a fellow creator. You know firsthand how it's a cycle of feeling totally filled up and utterly drained out...

Way to complete an Advent,
@Starbird_Resources
!  I dig those round windows with the spikey bits and the multicoloured candles. ^_^

Love the furniture variations, and the carpets on Day 12 are a really nice addition to interior decor too! Thanks,
@Starbird_Resources
- it's been fun seeing what you've made every day for the past few weeks, and there are so many useful and beautiful items. Happy holidays to you too!

@MrKEK
that is amazing! Thank you so much!! I'm sorry I didn't see your post back when made it -- just started a new job and have been busy. But that is so cool, I love it. And thanks so much for sharing it with the community.
This totally made my day

